<!--==========PLANT BREEDING: 1.4 (as of 10.12.26)==========

Organic plant breeding allows players to combine two plants, or one plant + one special sap, to create a new plant.
Aquiring new plants is handled via existing crafting methods:
	-The player will need have one of the ingredient seeds.
	-Plants capable of creating new seeds will sometimes create a special 'essence'. This essence is then combined with the seed.
	-Some seeds just need to be infused with sap to create new plants.
-Plant sizes range from 1x1 to 9x9, though they will generally be 1x1, 2x2, or 3x3.
-Generally these plants are NOT considered 'super', and may die out to natural causes.
-New plants are a mix of cosmetic, producing specific resources, or creating special trees entirely.
-Examples of plants that can be created are:
	-Glowberry Bushes, which are created by combining blueberries + glowsap. A food enjoyed by those with organic implants.
	-Chronosap recipes that accelerate evolving trees to their higher stages
	-Creating a weep focused on producing only endosap.
	-Plants that will hyperpopulate the surrounding area with a specific crop
	-Defensive trees that can plant both prima and perennial turrets.
	-Creating trees that provide bonuses from other paths (i.e. lightning or fire)
	-Gauranlen Magnus, an offbreed Guaranlen Tree that can also produce Gau weapons.
	-Trees intended to grow specifically pretty/unique wood types (generally with good stats or special graphics).



-Many trees require essence to acquire:
	-Trees that get stronger require essence of it's previous 'tier'.
	-Some trees focused on stats (beauty, resistances, textures, etc.) will need essence.


-Plants that focus on stats generally start off with the technology itself. The player's first stat trees start with wood + saps. For example:
	-Wood + Brightsap: Shimmertree Seed.
	-Wood + Endosap: Greenshield Seed: Wood with high durability and much lower flammability.
	-Player then grows the Greenshield Tree, And will have to wait an indeterminate amount of time until it produces the Essence of the Greenshield.
	-Player can now combine the Greenshield Essence with other seeds, i.e. a Shimmertree Seed. This now produces the Hardlight Tree, and the cycle continues.
	-The opposite is also true: player can grow a Shimmertree seed, get it's essence, and combine it with a Greenshield Sapling. The result will be the same.

-Plants that produce resources and create other plants often need two plants made with the sap; one statistical, and one gated in progression.
	-Player wants to produce constant endosap
	-Greenshield OR Shimmertree Essence can work since they utilize endosap.
	-Player also needs to make a new plant using Perennial tech.
	-Perennial Wood + Endosap: Silverwall Tree. Grows sections of strong periwood wall automatically.
	-Player will now need to combine the essence of one with the other to get to new resource provider.


-Plants utilizing DLC trees will need the seed, or genetic material, of the DLC plant. It will also need a very specific rare sap.
	-Anima Tree Essence + Summersap. The anima tree can 'consume' psychic energy over a period of time, causing a variety of map effects. This ranges from arti
		-New Anima tree also grows berries over time
	-Gauranlen Tree Seed + Springsap





