=====Anything marked 'Incomplete' will be added as soon as possible, while anything marked 'delayed' will be added in a larger future update.=====

=====SUMMARY=====
-Basic and advanced metal reclamation is part of Ferrokinesis; once those two are researched, the player will need to dedicate themselves to the study.
	-The player needs Chronite and Embersap at minimum for further creations. Various processors will still be used, divided by item type: wearables, weapons, basic items, and advanced items. They always melt down into their dominant material.
	-The next processors are multi-tile forges that melt down anything within a 3x3 - 7x7 space. They produce an immense amount of heat around themselves, are always running, but are more efficient and can produce two ingredients instead of one.
	-Later processors can produce gold, silver, uranium, etc. from specific items. Eventually a vat can be created that produces vivium.



=====TIER 1 FERROKINESIS=====

-Enables the three 1x1 processor forges.
	-Each item melts into it's dominant material. 
	-A way to extract embersap is expected by this point.
	-Materials stop at their base component; they cannot be reduced further.

=====TIER 2 FERROKINESIS=====

-Enables the 3x3 multi-tile forge.
-Processors can now break down uncraftable items.
-Midas tech begins at this point.

=====TIER 3 FERROKINESIS=====

-Enables the 5x5 multi-tile forge.
-Processors can now break down natural geo materials (stones and metals) into terrasalts
-New alchemic benches can create other natural materials at a 70:30 ratio.
-Steel and plasteel can be melted and shaped into compact canisters that can be sold or stored.

=====TIER 4 FERROKINESIS=====

-Enables the 7x7 multi-tile forge.
-Processors can now break down synthetic geo materials (plasteel and steel) into terrasalts
-Cross-compatibility with other paths is now possible.
-New alchemic bench now has an efficiency of 40:60.

